<title>SINGAPORE: Taiwan ups June fuel oil bunker prices by $2/T.</title>
<headline>Taiwan ups June fuel oil bunker prices by $2/T.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-07-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's Chinese Petroleum Corp (CPC) has raised its bunker fuel prices by $2 per tonne effective June 27, a company statement said on Monday.</p>
<p>Posted prices for 180, 280 and 380-centistoke bunker fuel delivered at the ports of Keelung, Hualien, Taichung and Suao were raised by $2 to $119 per tonne.</p>
<p>Term prices were also raised by $2 to $116 per tonne.</p>
<p>CPC is Taiwan's monopoly supplier of bunker fuels.</p>
<p>-- Singapore Newsroom (+65-870 3571)</p>
</text>
